New: WOOX M-LOK Leather Cartridge Quiver

New: WOOX M-LOK Leather Cartridge Quiver

WOOX’s $69 six-round carrier takes the company’s polymer M-LOK quiver and rebuilds it in handmade Italian leather.

SSUSA Staff

WOOX already sells a six-round M-LOK cartridge quiver, a $49 polymer piece finished in Cerakote. Its newest one does the same job in leather for $20 more.

The M-LOK Leather Cartridge Quiver is made by hand in Naples from Tuscan leather, and the side that sits against the gun is lined with suede. A metal core inside gives it structure, with six cartridges in an elastic retention system.

Installation takes two free M-LOK slots, and that’s the catch for a lot of traditional rifles. Many walnut-stocked lever guns don’t have any. WOOX, unsurprisingly, has an answer in its own catalog. Its Bravado stock for Henry and Marlin lever actions has a two-slot M-LOK rail on the right side of the buttstock, put there for quivers and similar add-ons, and the matching handguard carries slots at 3, 6 and 9 o'clock.

WOOX also sells a $149 leather quiver that laces onto bolt-action stocks and holds five rounds.

According to the company, the elastic on the M-LOK model will take .223 Rem., .300 BLK, .30-30 Win., .45-70 Gov't, .357 Mag., .44 Mag. and .45 Colt.

Find it listed on wooxstore.com at $69.

